WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:03.003
[♪ theme music playing]

00:29.112 --> 00:30.197
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:33.283 --> 00:34.826
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:34.910 --> 00:36.203
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:36.286 --> 00:37.287
EPISODE 9

00:37.371 --> 00:39.039
[man on phone]
Hello, this is the restaurant, Naum.

00:39.122 --> 00:41.166
We found your pen while cleaning.

00:41.250 --> 00:45.212
If you ever find it,
can you contact me through this number?

00:45.295 --> 00:49.216
[man] I remembered that you asked us
to contact you if we ever found it.

00:49.299 --> 00:51.301
[♪ sentimental music playing]

00:54.596 --> 00:57.182
I think you owe me an explanation.

01:00.352 --> 01:02.437
[high-pitched ringing]

01:11.613 --> 01:12.906
[breathes heavily]

01:12.990 --> 01:15.117
[Haran] The location of the engraving,
and the font.

01:15.200 --> 01:17.202
Both of them are my pen.

01:17.286 --> 01:18.453
How can this happen?

01:19.705 --> 01:20.706
I…

01:21.957 --> 01:23.709
[hesitates] I bought it before.

01:23.792 --> 01:24.835
What do you mean?

01:25.586 --> 01:26.920
How could you have--

01:27.004 --> 01:28.297
I bought the same pen

01:30.507 --> 01:32.092
when I was in the States.

01:33.719 --> 01:36.138
When I first ran into you at the atelier,

01:36.221 --> 01:38.765
I was shocked when I saw your pen

01:38.849 --> 01:40.809
because it was so familiar.

01:46.023 --> 01:48.608
So you bought it when you returned
to the States?

01:48.692 --> 01:49.818
You got the same one?

01:51.611 --> 01:52.612
Yes.

01:54.614 --> 01:55.615
[sighs]

01:56.450 --> 01:59.494
You should've told me.
I was so confused when I got this.

02:01.455 --> 02:04.249
I thought it was a special pen
made just for me,

02:05.208 --> 02:07.252
but I guess it's common in the US.

02:08.920 --> 02:10.547
You could've said you bought it.

02:10.630 --> 02:12.466
Did you think I'd feel uncomfortable?

02:13.884 --> 02:17.262
You really are an artist,
paying attention to so much detail.

02:17.346 --> 02:19.014
The engraving's exactly the same.

02:19.598 --> 02:23.810
It's just like you to go
and buy another one for me.

02:25.979 --> 02:27.022
I'm sorry.

02:28.899 --> 02:29.900
I…

02:34.905 --> 02:36.031
lied to you.

02:36.114 --> 02:37.908
You did it for me.

02:37.991 --> 02:39.493
I'll use it well. Thank you.

02:40.535 --> 02:42.079
It might be an ordinary pen,

02:42.162 --> 02:45.040
but the thought
behind buying it for me is special.

02:45.832 --> 02:47.000
So thank you.

02:48.251 --> 02:50.253
[♪ music fades]

02:50.337 --> 02:52.047
What is it this time?

02:52.130 --> 02:54.091
What on earth is going on with you?

02:59.137 --> 03:00.138
Mmm...

03:00.222 --> 03:01.348
You caught me.

03:03.141 --> 03:04.142
[sniffles]

03:04.893 --> 03:06.186
I'm going to France soon.

03:06.269 --> 03:07.521
France?

03:08.647 --> 03:09.648
When?

03:09.731 --> 03:11.942
Probably before spring.

03:12.025 --> 03:13.860
[sighs deeply]

03:13.944 --> 03:15.028
Spring?

03:16.238 --> 03:20.242
I was planning on retiring and going there
when I was around 60.

03:20.325 --> 03:23.537
But my plans got postponed
because of my daughter and son-in-law.

03:24.579 --> 03:27.165
I haven't told the kids yet,

03:28.792 --> 03:30.544
but I really want a break now.

03:30.627 --> 03:33.839
I've been working my butt off
for the past 50 years.

03:34.840 --> 03:35.841
Is that…

03:36.716 --> 03:37.717
really it?

03:38.176 --> 03:39.177
Of course.

03:39.261 --> 03:40.262
[♪ emotional music playing]

03:40.345 --> 03:42.347
I wish I'd reunited with you sooner.

03:43.557 --> 03:44.558
It's just too bad.

03:45.851 --> 03:47.853
I have a lot on my mind these days.

03:48.353 --> 03:50.272
There's so much
to take care of before I go.

03:50.355 --> 03:52.441
That's why I wanted to go
to Chuncheon soon.

03:52.524 --> 03:53.692
Why did you go to the hospital?

03:55.235 --> 03:56.611
You weren't visiting a friend.

03:56.695 --> 03:59.364
I saw a nurse…

04:01.408 --> 04:02.409
calling your name.

04:02.492 --> 04:03.493
[chuckles softly]

04:03.994 --> 04:06.580
You think it's easy
managing a company until this age?

04:07.080 --> 04:10.125
My health is my asset,
so I get regular checkups.

04:10.208 --> 04:11.543
I just didn't want you to worry.

04:12.794 --> 04:15.046
Anyway, let's go to Chuncheon soon.

04:17.215 --> 04:20.385
I wonder if our house is still there.
[giggles]

04:23.513 --> 04:25.766
[♪ music fades]

04:38.612 --> 04:40.280
[♪ gentle music playing]

04:40.363 --> 04:41.698
[sighs]

04:41.782 --> 04:43.158
This is it.

05:22.697 --> 05:24.449
You did it for me.

05:24.533 --> 05:25.826
So thank you.

05:26.618 --> 05:30.497
[Chan] The more you gain with deception,

05:30.580 --> 05:32.582
the less you can truly gain.

05:32.666 --> 05:34.751
It may seem like
you're gaining something now,

05:34.835 --> 05:37.212
but you'll probably end up
paying the price for it.

05:37.295 --> 05:38.797
[inhales]

05:39.923 --> 05:41.383
[tuts, sighs in frustration]

05:44.135 --> 05:45.178
[metallic clink]

05:47.222 --> 05:49.307
[door opens, closes]

06:00.235 --> 06:01.361
[metallic clink]

06:07.075 --> 06:09.452
[metallic clinking echoes]

06:09.536 --> 06:10.662
[groans softly]

06:10.745 --> 06:13.164
-[rapid metallic clink echoes]
-[groans]

06:14.541 --> 06:16.001
[toy squeaks]

06:16.084 --> 06:18.086
[breathing heavily]

06:18.169 --> 06:20.171
[♪ emotional music playing]

06:22.465 --> 06:25.051
-[toy squeaks]
-[panting]

06:30.265 --> 06:31.266
[Chan] The price…

06:37.230 --> 06:39.482
[♪ music swells, fades]

06:39.566 --> 06:42.152
-[leaves rustling]
-[birds chirping]

06:42.235 --> 06:44.154
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

06:44.237 --> 06:45.530
[sizzling]

06:45.614 --> 06:47.866
[Hayeong] Gosh, that's hot! I almost died.

06:47.949 --> 06:49.993
[objects clattering]

06:50.076 --> 06:51.244
[mumbles] Be quiet…

06:57.417 --> 06:58.460
[sighs]

07:04.382 --> 07:05.425
The porridge.

07:05.508 --> 07:06.885
[Taeseok sighs wearily]

07:14.643 --> 07:15.644
Ms. Song?

07:16.353 --> 07:18.271
[exclaims] You're awake.

07:18.355 --> 07:19.689
-What are you doing here?
-[Hayeong] Uh...

07:19.773 --> 07:22.317
I came to drop off some documents,

07:22.400 --> 07:23.860
but I guess you don't remember.

07:23.943 --> 07:25.362
Are you feeling better?

07:25.945 --> 07:26.988
What is all this?

07:27.072 --> 07:30.909
How can you only have water
and candy at home?

07:30.992 --> 07:34.579
So I ordered some pots
and dishes and stuff.

07:35.038 --> 07:36.456
Delivery is awesome in Korea!

07:37.332 --> 07:38.833
Sit down. The porridge is done.

07:39.334 --> 07:41.419
It's late. You should go.

07:42.003 --> 07:43.129
-I'll take you--
-[Hayeong exclaims]

07:43.213 --> 07:45.048
Don't be silly. You're sick.

07:47.092 --> 07:51.304
There's nothing more miserable
than being alone when you're sick.

07:51.388 --> 07:52.972
So stay right here.

07:53.515 --> 07:55.517
Ah, pardon me for a moment.

07:57.477 --> 07:59.145
Okay. Your fever dropped.

07:59.229 --> 08:02.440
The pear tea's almost done, too.
It's the best for a cold.

08:05.026 --> 08:07.320
[Hyunwoo]
I don't think I should see Hayeong.

08:07.404 --> 08:09.030
She kept talking about you.

08:09.739 --> 08:11.324
I think she likes you a lot.

08:11.825 --> 08:12.909
[♪ sentimental music playing]

08:12.992 --> 08:14.452
[Hayeong exclaims] Really?

08:14.536 --> 08:17.163
-Top of his year the whole time?
-Yes. The entire time.

08:17.247 --> 08:19.040
Wow. He was a genius.

08:19.124 --> 08:21.376
His nickname was Yeon Taeseop,

08:21.459 --> 08:23.878
like Song Taeseop from Slam Dunk.

08:23.962 --> 08:24.963
[both laughing]

08:25.046 --> 08:28.216
Yeon Taeseop? So?
Did he enter competitions and stuff?

08:28.299 --> 08:30.593
[Hyunwoo] Of course. For competitions, he…

08:32.178 --> 08:34.806
Here. Unfortunately,
I can't guarantee the taste.

08:36.641 --> 08:37.976
I'll eat it when you leave.

08:38.059 --> 08:40.145
-It's late, so--
-No.

08:40.228 --> 08:42.230
I'll leave after I see you
finishing the bowl.

08:43.189 --> 08:47.277
You were the one who told me
to be honest if I wasn't okay.

08:47.360 --> 08:49.612
Why didn't you tell me you were sick?

08:50.280 --> 08:51.281
I…

08:52.365 --> 08:54.159
shouldn't be sick.

08:54.242 --> 08:55.243
Huh?

08:55.326 --> 08:57.203
Why would anyone
not be allowed to be sick?

08:57.287 --> 08:58.496
You just have to get better.

08:59.330 --> 09:00.457
Eat up before it gets cold.

09:02.208 --> 09:03.209
All right.

09:09.716 --> 09:10.717
Mr. Yeon.

09:11.342 --> 09:13.762
I'll get straight to the point.

09:14.846 --> 09:17.724
I've been getting my hopes up these days.

09:18.683 --> 09:21.311
I thought you were blushing and sweating

09:22.145 --> 09:25.440
because you had feelings for me.
I didn't know you were sick.

09:25.523 --> 09:28.026
But to be honest,

09:28.985 --> 09:29.986
I was happy.

09:31.654 --> 09:35.658
Mr. Yeon, even seeing you with bedhead
makes me curious.

09:35.742 --> 09:38.995
I find myself overthinking
everything you do or say.

09:39.079 --> 09:41.372
And it hurts to see you sick.

09:41.831 --> 09:44.084
I guess I've been denying my feelings,

09:44.167 --> 09:46.044
but I'm sure of it now.

09:46.753 --> 09:48.379
-Mr. Yeon.
-Ms. Song.

09:48.463 --> 09:50.048
I think I like you.

09:50.131 --> 09:51.591
No, I'm sure I like you.

09:57.222 --> 09:58.223
If…

09:59.224 --> 10:01.851
I gave you the wrong idea, I'm sorry.

10:03.311 --> 10:06.523
But I've never thought of you…

10:08.775 --> 10:09.943
as more than a colleague.

10:10.026 --> 10:11.694
Yes, of course.

10:12.320 --> 10:13.530
I thought so.

10:13.613 --> 10:14.697
Mmm...

10:14.781 --> 10:15.782
Then…

10:17.742 --> 10:19.119
start thinking of me that way.

10:19.202 --> 10:21.412
[♪ heart-fluttering music playing]

10:22.080 --> 10:26.167
I guess you'll only eat comfortably
once I'm gone.

10:26.251 --> 10:30.088
[chuckles] Then I hope you get well soon.

10:30.171 --> 10:31.631
I'll see you at work.

10:33.967 --> 10:35.260
Ms. Song.

10:35.343 --> 10:37.345
[♪ heart-fluttering music continues]

10:45.687 --> 10:48.398
[Hayeong] Don't forget
to take this three times a day.

10:55.029 --> 10:56.030
[exhales]

10:56.114 --> 10:57.323
I must be crazy.

10:58.032 --> 10:59.534
I told him I like him.

11:01.327 --> 11:04.164
But it's fine.
I was just telling him the truth.

11:05.081 --> 11:06.374
Good job, Song Hayeong.

11:06.958 --> 11:09.252
[inhales, squeals]

11:09.335 --> 11:11.296
What do I do?

11:14.591 --> 11:16.593
[♪ music fades]

11:30.857 --> 11:32.692
[Hadam muttering] Please let Yougyum…

11:34.152 --> 11:35.945
be okay.

11:37.655 --> 11:38.865
Please…

11:38.948 --> 11:40.700
[Yougyum's father] Good job, Yougyum.

11:41.534 --> 11:43.995
[Hadam gasps] Yougyum, your foot.

11:44.078 --> 11:45.496
[breath trembling]

11:46.998 --> 11:47.999
What did they say?

11:50.960 --> 11:52.670
I've recovered. [chuckles]

11:52.754 --> 11:55.173
I'll be perfectly healed
after some treatment.

11:56.049 --> 11:58.134
It must have swollen from exhaustion.

11:58.718 --> 12:00.637
I'll be fine in a week.

12:00.762 --> 12:03.514
-You must have been shocked.
-[sighs in relief]

12:03.598 --> 12:05.225
[Yougyum's father exclaims]

12:05.308 --> 12:06.893
I'm so relieved.

12:07.685 --> 12:09.854
You were in the nurse's office
because of your foot, right?

12:09.938 --> 12:11.981
-[♪ amusing music playing]
-It was my fault.

12:12.065 --> 12:14.609
I misunderstood and threw a fit,

12:14.692 --> 12:16.653
and I made you worry about me.

12:16.736 --> 12:18.404
-[Hadam exhales]
-[Yougyum] Goodness.

12:18.488 --> 12:20.698
I thought you were smart,
but you were a fool.

12:21.407 --> 12:22.617
That's nonsense.

12:22.700 --> 12:25.411
[voice shaking] I thought you wouldn't
be able to play baseball again.

12:25.495 --> 12:27.622
Hadam! It's an emergency. Get up.

12:27.705 --> 12:30.124
What is it? Is your foot hurting?

12:30.208 --> 12:31.334
No.

12:32.168 --> 12:35.922
You're wasting your time here
when the CSAT is just around the corner.

12:36.005 --> 12:38.591
Hurry home and get some rest.

12:38.675 --> 12:40.343
I'm going to nurse you.

12:40.426 --> 12:41.552
Really?

12:42.178 --> 12:44.472
Then I should go home
instead of getting treated.

12:45.139 --> 12:47.517
Okay, fine. I'll go.

12:47.600 --> 12:51.729
Don't worry, and focus on the CSAT.
We'll take good care of him.

12:51.813 --> 12:54.857
Don't think about coming before the exams.
I won't even let you in.

12:54.941 --> 12:57.986
I'll get plenty of rest
and receive treatment.

12:58.069 --> 13:00.113
So let's meet after the exams, okay?

13:00.196 --> 13:01.823
[♪ music fades]

13:01.906 --> 13:03.074
Focus!

13:03.157 --> 13:04.617
Focus. [sniffling]

13:06.911 --> 13:09.372
I want you in charge of this.

13:09.455 --> 13:11.457
The overall visuals
for a fashion editorial?

13:11.541 --> 13:13.084
You always did this yourself…

13:13.167 --> 13:16.045
This shoot is about showcasing
the brand's identity.

13:16.129 --> 13:19.757
It's about time
we aligned it with your pace.

13:20.383 --> 13:23.261
Plan the mood, color scheme,
and the flow of the looks.

13:23.344 --> 13:26.014
As you said, we're showcasing
the brand's overall tone.

13:26.097 --> 13:27.098
You should handle--

13:27.181 --> 13:29.642
What do you think, Mr. Yeon?
Will it be hard for her?

13:30.226 --> 13:32.729
I believe she can do it.

13:32.812 --> 13:35.023
I'll support you with anything you need.

13:35.106 --> 13:36.482
Okay. Then that's done.

13:36.566 --> 13:41.237
From now on, prioritize Ms. Song's opinion
when adjusting colors and quantities.

13:41.320 --> 13:43.990
What? Ms. Kim…

13:44.073 --> 13:45.283
Why are you--

13:45.366 --> 13:46.784
Don't make me repeat myself.

13:47.618 --> 13:49.746
You should take some of my workload.

13:49.829 --> 13:51.706
Let me get some rest, too.

13:52.290 --> 13:55.084
Ah. And clear my schedule
for a day this week.

13:55.168 --> 13:56.419
-Is there something…
-What…

13:57.962 --> 13:59.005
Go ahead.

14:00.048 --> 14:01.090
Is something wrong?

14:01.174 --> 14:03.092
You never asked
to clear a schedule before.

14:03.176 --> 14:06.763
It's just that I want some fresh air
before it gets too cold.

14:06.846 --> 14:09.140
-Then I'll take you--
-It's fine. I can go on my own.

14:10.808 --> 14:11.893
Yes, ma'am.

14:11.976 --> 14:13.061
But, Ms. Kim,

14:13.144 --> 14:14.729
-I really don't think I should do--
-[Nana claps]

14:14.812 --> 14:15.980
Meeting's over.

14:18.566 --> 14:19.901
[sighs]

14:19.984 --> 14:21.819
[♪ emotional music playing]

14:27.366 --> 14:28.910
Will I have enough time?

14:30.328 --> 14:31.329
No.

14:32.747 --> 14:34.415
I have to get it done.

14:40.630 --> 14:42.965
Uh, she has a personal appointment.

14:43.508 --> 14:45.927
All right.
Please postpone it to next week.

14:46.886 --> 14:47.887
[clears throat]

14:49.013 --> 14:50.973
Good afternoon.

14:51.808 --> 14:53.351
Are you feeling better?

14:54.143 --> 14:55.770
-Yes, thanks to you.
-[elevator dings]

14:57.355 --> 14:58.397
[Hayeong sighs]

15:02.777 --> 15:06.405
Song Hayeong, age 29, ENFP.
And ENFJ when I'm working.

15:06.948 --> 15:10.785
I like my family, friends,
colleagues, work, driving,

15:10.868 --> 15:12.787
listening to music while walking
on a windy day,

15:12.870 --> 15:14.122
being honest, tasty food,

15:14.205 --> 15:15.581
especially snack bar food.

15:15.665 --> 15:17.959
Mmm... And watching
cute videos before bed.

15:18.042 --> 15:19.585
[♪ amusing music playing]

15:19.669 --> 15:21.254
-What?
-And what I don't like

15:21.337 --> 15:22.755
are people who are frustrating,

15:22.839 --> 15:26.134
cowardly, who pick on the weak,
stir up conflict, snitch, get paranoid.

15:26.217 --> 15:27.760
And I hate losing people I love,

15:27.844 --> 15:29.595
seeing them in pain...

15:30.138 --> 15:32.265
Ah, and mosquitoes.

15:33.724 --> 15:36.727
Oh, and I forgot one.

15:36.811 --> 15:40.606
Recently, something was added
to the list of things I like.

15:42.984 --> 15:45.820
-[elevator dings]
-What are you doing?

15:48.197 --> 15:50.283
We don't know much
about each other personally,

15:50.366 --> 15:52.076
even after all these years.

15:52.160 --> 15:55.496
I told you to think about me,
but I thought you wouldn't have much info,

15:55.580 --> 15:57.165
so I gave you some.

16:03.421 --> 16:05.214
Ah, I'm not pressuring you.

16:05.298 --> 16:08.718
You're always serious and prudent,
so you can take your time.

16:08.801 --> 16:10.428
It's all right with me.

16:10.511 --> 16:13.973
But everyone ends up liking me
the more they get to know me.

16:14.056 --> 16:16.475
I'm just saying.

16:17.602 --> 16:21.022
Having personal conversations
like this at work isn't really…

16:21.105 --> 16:22.148
[Hayeong exclaims]

16:22.773 --> 16:26.277
Mr. Yeon doesn't like
personal conversations at work.

16:27.153 --> 16:28.279
[in English] Okay.

16:28.362 --> 16:31.199
[in Korean] I just acquired
some more info about you.

16:32.074 --> 16:34.035
Then have a good day.

16:36.412 --> 16:38.414
[♪ music fades]

16:40.458 --> 16:42.293
[♪ pleasant music playing]

16:42.376 --> 16:44.462
[Chan in English]
So, what do you think about this scene?

16:44.545 --> 16:47.173
[Ben] Um...
Yeah, I mean, it's good overall.

16:47.256 --> 16:48.716
A few things here and there
we could tweak.

16:48.799 --> 16:51.552
[in Korean] Oh! Ben, how have you been?

16:51.636 --> 16:54.013
I've been doing very well. [chuckles]

16:54.096 --> 16:57.308
My mother-in-law's food is amazing.
[laughs]

16:57.391 --> 17:01.062
We were having a meeting
because we got the additional script.

17:01.604 --> 17:03.481
We'll send it to the design team later.

17:03.564 --> 17:05.858
All right. I'll let you work.
[chuckles softly]

17:07.193 --> 17:08.194
Hi.

17:09.028 --> 17:10.029
[Ben in English] Sounds good.

17:13.115 --> 17:14.617
[sighs]

17:15.451 --> 17:16.494
Good meeting.

17:16.577 --> 17:18.079
[lively chatter]

17:18.162 --> 17:19.747
[in Korean]
Should I raise the neckline a bit?

17:19.830 --> 17:21.332
[Ben and Chan laughing]

17:22.833 --> 17:24.210
Mr. Park, the coffee.

17:24.293 --> 17:25.294
[Manjae] Oh, gosh.

17:25.378 --> 17:26.379
Goodness.

17:27.713 --> 17:29.215
Uh, were you looking at this pen?

17:30.132 --> 17:32.552
Mr. Seonu bought this for me.
[chuckles softly]

17:32.635 --> 17:34.637
This must be common in the States.

17:34.720 --> 17:37.223
He got it for me
when he went back last time.

17:37.306 --> 17:39.350
He even put a lucky sticker on it.

17:39.433 --> 17:41.018
Right… [chuckles nervously]

17:41.102 --> 17:43.688
I'm glad you like it.

17:44.689 --> 17:45.690
[sighs]

17:47.900 --> 17:51.487
[♪ J.S. Bach "Goldberg Variations,
BWV 988: Aria" playing on speakers]

17:58.744 --> 18:00.204
I guess you like Bach.

18:00.288 --> 18:03.666
No. I just happened
to hear about the song.

18:03.749 --> 18:07.044
Someone told me it's good for insomnia.

18:17.013 --> 18:18.431
[Manjae] The music is a bit sad.

18:18.973 --> 18:21.225
I should change it to a brighter song.

18:22.768 --> 18:24.312
-[inhales sharply]
-[♪ music stops]

18:30.526 --> 18:32.612
[♪ pleasant jazz music
playing on speakers]

18:35.781 --> 18:38.034
[Manjae] Let her feel joy again.

18:39.076 --> 18:42.580
Tell me anything. I'll be your safe space.

18:46.917 --> 18:48.461
[cellphone vibrates]

18:50.546 --> 18:52.715
[Hadam] Ta-da! I'm getting perfect scores.

18:52.798 --> 18:54.216
I'm going to nail the CSAT.

18:54.300 --> 18:57.053
How are you feeling? Is the food okay?

18:57.136 --> 19:00.097
[Yougyum] Ta-da! I'm cleaning
all my plates, and I'm in great condition!

19:00.181 --> 19:02.183
Don't worry about me and focus.

19:02.850 --> 19:04.101
Hmm!

19:04.185 --> 19:05.186
Right. Focus.

19:08.439 --> 19:10.399
[Chan murmuring in English]
"Won flew through the night sky.

19:10.483 --> 19:14.362
"Below her, the Milky Way
was pouring down like a river."

19:14.445 --> 19:15.905
Milky Way…

19:15.988 --> 19:18.449
Won flew through the night sky.

19:18.991 --> 19:24.455
Below her, the Milky Way
was pouring down like a river.

19:25.456 --> 19:26.457
[Chan exclaims]

19:29.669 --> 19:31.087
[inhales sharply]

19:38.886 --> 19:40.971
[cellphone vibrating]

19:41.055 --> 19:42.056
Hmm?

19:42.139 --> 19:44.558
RAN

19:44.642 --> 19:45.893
You haven't gone to bed?

19:45.976 --> 19:47.061
Not yet.

19:47.144 --> 19:48.813
[♪ gentle music playing]

19:50.523 --> 19:51.899
But what are you up to?

19:51.982 --> 19:54.318
There's a newly added scene
of the Milky Way,

19:54.944 --> 19:56.529
so I wanted to go see it.

19:57.279 --> 19:58.406
Should we…

19:59.907 --> 20:01.951
Oh, it's pretty late.

20:02.034 --> 20:03.786
[Haran] Driving alone at this hour?

20:04.453 --> 20:07.832
That's not fair. We promised
to work through your list together.

20:07.915 --> 20:09.792
Stargazing was on your list.

20:09.875 --> 20:13.087
Going alone doesn't count.
I'll take my car and head there.

20:13.170 --> 20:14.255
So just wait.

20:15.715 --> 20:16.882
[Chan exclaims]

20:16.966 --> 20:20.344
I guess the moon's in a good mood today.

20:20.886 --> 20:23.264
We won't be able to see the Milky Way
if it's so bright.

20:23.347 --> 20:24.473
Hmm?

20:24.557 --> 20:26.475
We can't see it because of the moon?

20:27.101 --> 20:29.061
The moon's pretty bright,

20:29.687 --> 20:33.357
so faint lights like the Milky Way
get washed out by the light.

20:33.941 --> 20:35.526
Oh...

20:35.609 --> 20:37.069
[coughs]

20:37.153 --> 20:38.154
It's cold, isn't it?

20:38.654 --> 20:39.947
Sorry, it's my fault.

20:41.657 --> 20:43.284
Uh, can we use that?

20:46.954 --> 20:47.955
-Here.
-Thanks.

20:49.165 --> 20:50.249
[Chan groans]

20:50.875 --> 20:52.376
[hesitates] Let's just go.

20:52.460 --> 20:54.378
We'll come back
when the moon's less bright.

20:55.629 --> 20:56.881
Oh! [gasps]

20:59.842 --> 21:01.010
[sighs in relief]

21:01.093 --> 21:02.094
[exclaims]

21:02.178 --> 21:04.180
[♪ fantastical music playing]

21:05.389 --> 21:06.390
[both exclaim]

21:07.767 --> 21:10.186
[both chuckle softly]

21:10.269 --> 21:11.937
[giggles]

21:21.739 --> 21:22.740
[camera shutter clicks]

21:23.532 --> 21:26.035
[Haran exclaims] It's so beautiful.

21:27.953 --> 21:28.954
[camera shutter clicks]

21:35.044 --> 21:37.546
[camera shutter clicking]

21:39.632 --> 21:42.551
[exhales] I feel like I'm in space.

21:43.677 --> 21:45.846
I feel like I'm in a dream.

21:52.853 --> 21:53.854
[Chan clears throat]

22:03.781 --> 22:04.782
[Haran chuckles]

22:07.368 --> 22:08.452
But…

22:09.745 --> 22:12.665
those words sounded a bit sad.

22:14.166 --> 22:16.919
The Milky Way being visible
when there's no moon.

22:17.002 --> 22:18.838
[♪ music fades]

22:18.921 --> 22:22.675
The moon and the Milky Way
go so well together.

22:24.218 --> 22:29.306
It sounds like
they're not meant to be together.

22:31.058 --> 22:34.228
Hmm... That's a bit sad. [chuckles softly]

22:35.813 --> 22:39.525
[sighs deeply]
I feel like I'll never be able

22:40.150 --> 22:42.027
[echoing, muffled]
...to forget this moment.

22:42.111 --> 22:43.320
[high-pitched ringing]

22:43.404 --> 22:45.739
I've never really liked winter...

22:46.365 --> 22:47.783
[silence]

23:01.463 --> 23:02.464
Don't you think so?

23:02.548 --> 23:04.300
-[gasps]
-[♪ melancholic music playing]

23:04.383 --> 23:05.384
Hmm?

23:05.467 --> 23:06.760
You were distracted, weren't you?

23:06.844 --> 23:09.722
[chuckles wryly] Sorry.

23:09.805 --> 23:13.559
The stars and the person next to me

23:13.642 --> 23:14.894
were so beautiful

23:15.728 --> 23:17.897
that I spaced out for a moment.

23:17.980 --> 23:19.023
-[chuckles nervously]
-[scoffs]

23:19.106 --> 23:20.274
Gosh.

23:22.067 --> 23:25.070
I said I won't ever forget

23:25.821 --> 23:27.781
this moment.

23:29.658 --> 23:32.328
Ah, and in spring…

23:33.329 --> 23:35.247
Uh, will you not be here in spring?

23:38.792 --> 23:39.793
Anyway,

23:40.836 --> 23:41.837
thank you

23:42.713 --> 23:44.465
for showing me such a beautiful sky.

23:47.718 --> 23:49.470
[exhales]

23:59.396 --> 24:02.650
-[Manjae coughing]
-[♪ music fades]

24:03.525 --> 24:06.403
You're back late. You look tired.

24:06.487 --> 24:07.696
Go and rest.

24:07.780 --> 24:09.239
Goodnight.

24:11.742 --> 24:13.744
[water pouring]

24:15.621 --> 24:16.622
Mr. Park.

24:17.665 --> 24:18.666
Yes?

24:19.625 --> 24:20.626
I…

24:22.461 --> 24:24.171
want to stay by her side

24:25.923 --> 24:28.634
in spring, in summer,

24:30.844 --> 24:32.262
in fall, and in winter.

24:32.346 --> 24:34.348
[♪ emotional music playing]

24:35.975 --> 24:37.226
I want…

24:41.397 --> 24:43.440
to stay by her side,

24:46.485 --> 24:48.237
but I don't know what to do.

24:58.080 --> 24:59.248
Do you need someone

25:00.332 --> 25:01.458
to talk to?

25:05.587 --> 25:06.922
[sobs]

25:09.967 --> 25:11.969
[♪ emotional music continues]

25:21.729 --> 25:23.522
[Chan] "Surrounded by walls"?

25:24.565 --> 25:26.191
[laptop pinging]

25:26.275 --> 25:27.651
You saved me as well.

25:27.735 --> 25:29.403
Neon alien…

25:50.632 --> 25:52.843
-[♪ emotional music continues]
-[sighs]

25:52.926 --> 25:58.724
SUMMER, SEVEN YEARS AGO
IT STARTED WITH WALLS

26:03.187 --> 26:05.189
[♪ music fades]

26:06.732 --> 26:08.067
[Hayeong yawns]

26:08.150 --> 26:10.486
I heard you going out late last night.

26:10.986 --> 26:12.905
Were you meeting Chan?

26:12.988 --> 26:14.531
Just for a bit.

26:14.615 --> 26:18.452
Why did you meet at that hour?
Were you making out?

26:18.994 --> 26:20.037
Does it show?

26:21.205 --> 26:22.915
[gasps] Goodness.

26:22.998 --> 26:24.583
No, not at all.

26:24.666 --> 26:26.210
Good job. Make out as much as you want.

26:26.293 --> 26:27.461
[Hayeong gasps]

26:28.170 --> 26:29.963
You're coming downstairs already?

26:30.047 --> 26:31.840
[Haran] Did you not get enough sleep?

26:31.924 --> 26:34.551
I did, I went to bed
at 9:00p.m. last night.

26:35.302 --> 26:38.722
But what's going on here?

26:39.515 --> 26:42.559
Ta-da. We're making you
a lunchbox for your CSAT.

26:42.643 --> 26:46.063
We've been planning the menu
for the past three days.

26:46.146 --> 26:48.690
Will it be safe to eat?

26:48.774 --> 26:51.193
-Of course.
-I can just buy gimbap.

26:51.276 --> 26:53.487
Mom would scold us harshly
if you did that.

26:53.570 --> 26:55.280
Hang on. We just have to heat the soup.

26:55.364 --> 26:57.366
I have to go now, though.

26:57.449 --> 26:58.659
There's plenty of time.

26:58.742 --> 27:01.245
I want to visit Yougyum at the hospital
before I go.

27:01.328 --> 27:03.455
Hospital? Yougyum's in the hospital?

27:03.539 --> 27:06.083
[groans softly]
He told me not to say anything…

27:08.752 --> 27:11.421
He's hospitalized because of his foot.

27:11.505 --> 27:12.589
[Hayeong] Was he hurt badly?

27:12.673 --> 27:14.174
He's a baseball player--

27:14.258 --> 27:16.552
He said he'll get better
with some treatment,

27:17.427 --> 27:18.428
but I'm worried.

27:18.512 --> 27:19.513
[sighs]

27:20.055 --> 27:22.724
Anyway, he's my good luck charm,

27:22.808 --> 27:25.853
so I feel like I should see him
before the CSAT to do well.

27:25.936 --> 27:27.938
Hang on. I'll pack something for him, too.

27:28.647 --> 27:30.899
Hadam, come here for a moment.

27:31.650 --> 27:34.653
Sit down. I'll tie your hair for you.

27:35.696 --> 27:36.697
That's so random.

27:36.780 --> 27:38.657
-[Nana chuckles softly]
-[♪ gentle music playing]

27:38.740 --> 27:40.367
When you have a lot on your mind,

27:41.201 --> 27:43.161
brushing your hair calmly

27:43.745 --> 27:45.873
will help you relax.

27:49.167 --> 27:51.336
Yougyum will get through it,

27:52.045 --> 27:55.924
and don't forget
that you're perfectly prepared.

28:01.305 --> 28:02.639
You look beautiful.

28:02.723 --> 28:03.724
[Hadam chuckles]

28:04.433 --> 28:06.977
Of course. I'm your granddaughter.

28:10.564 --> 28:11.899
Don't worry.

28:12.482 --> 28:16.028
I'm your granddaughter,
and Haran and Hayeong's little sister.

28:16.904 --> 28:18.614
I'll do well.

28:18.697 --> 28:20.240
[Haran] We can take you.

28:20.324 --> 28:23.577
It's really fine.
I want to do this on my own.

28:24.953 --> 28:27.164
Our baby is all grown up
and taking the CSAT.

28:27.247 --> 28:28.665
-[chuckles softly]
-[Hayeong claps] Did you prepare

28:28.749 --> 28:30.459
your OMR marker and a clock?

28:30.542 --> 28:32.502
Markers, clocks, and hand warmers.

28:32.586 --> 28:35.964
You and even Mr. Yeon
gave me a whole heap of them.

28:36.548 --> 28:39.259
She should go now.
Come on, let's give her some strength.

28:39.343 --> 28:40.344
[whines]

28:40.427 --> 28:42.471
[in unison] Strength.

28:46.183 --> 28:47.184
[groans softly]

28:47.267 --> 28:49.519
He said I shouldn't come before the CSAT.

28:50.354 --> 28:52.272
But I have to see him, no matter what.

28:54.024 --> 28:56.485
The surgery is at 8:30 a.m.

28:56.568 --> 28:59.947
and we'll fill the top of the foot
with bone taken from the pelvis.

29:00.697 --> 29:01.782
Surgery?

29:04.493 --> 29:06.703
-You're getting surgery?
-Hadam.

29:06.787 --> 29:08.246
You said it'll get better soon.

29:08.330 --> 29:10.874
Would a bone graft heal in just a week?

29:11.375 --> 29:14.086
I'm sorry. Can I talk to my friend
for just a moment?

29:17.381 --> 29:19.758
It must have hurt so much.

29:20.384 --> 29:23.178
Why didn't you tell me anything?

29:23.261 --> 29:26.306
How could I do that
when you're facing something so important?

29:27.099 --> 29:29.017
I'm okay, so go take the exams.

29:29.101 --> 29:30.102
No,

29:31.144 --> 29:33.313
the most important thing to me is you.

29:33.897 --> 29:35.023
I'm staying by your side.

29:35.607 --> 29:36.775
Hadam.

29:36.858 --> 29:39.444
How can I focus on my exams
when you're getting surgery?

29:39.528 --> 29:41.947
I can enter college a year late.

29:42.531 --> 29:44.616
You can just take the bone from my pelvis.

29:44.700 --> 29:46.952
You play sports, but I just sit and study.

29:47.035 --> 29:48.078
This is why

29:48.829 --> 29:50.455
I couldn't tell you.

29:51.456 --> 29:54.042
If you do this, I can't keep seeing you.

29:54.126 --> 29:58.338
-I can take the CSAT next year.
-[Yougyum] No, that's not okay with me.

29:58.922 --> 29:59.923
I…

30:01.550 --> 30:03.552
want to be able to face you without guilt.

30:08.181 --> 30:09.182
What do we do?

30:09.266 --> 30:15.063
[sobbing] What if you end up
not being able to play baseball?

30:16.648 --> 30:17.649
Hadam.

30:18.942 --> 30:20.068
Give me your hand.

30:22.779 --> 30:25.073
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

30:25.157 --> 30:28.493
I'll recover perfectly
and be back on the mound soon.

30:28.577 --> 30:30.037
I'm just taking a short breather.

30:30.829 --> 30:32.039
You saw my room, right?

30:32.122 --> 30:35.625
My life's goal is to be someone
you can be proud of.

30:37.502 --> 30:38.628
[chuckles]

30:40.172 --> 30:44.217
Let's both focus on our own paths
and meet in a few hours.

30:44.301 --> 30:46.011
Come see me after the exams.

30:46.094 --> 30:47.262
You can do that, right?

30:56.229 --> 30:58.356
[teacher]
I'll distribute the exam papers now.

30:58.440 --> 31:01.526
Take one and pass them back.

31:20.962 --> 31:25.300
[Hadam]
Please let Yougyum's surgery go well.

31:27.469 --> 31:31.515
[Yougyum]
Please let Hadam do well on the exam.

31:31.598 --> 31:33.266
[♪ heartwarming music continuing]

31:34.518 --> 31:36.269
[teacher] Let's begin the test.

31:50.659 --> 31:52.953
SURGERY IN PROGRESS

31:53.036 --> 31:55.455
[♪ music fades]

31:55.539 --> 31:56.665
Good morning.

31:57.791 --> 31:59.376
And thank you.

32:00.293 --> 32:04.464
You really are considerate.
You send Hadam a clock and OMR markers.

32:04.548 --> 32:06.258
[snickers, inhales]

32:06.341 --> 32:07.467
What are you doing after work?

32:07.551 --> 32:09.636
I was thinking of getting snacks.

32:09.719 --> 32:11.346
-If you're free…
-[cellphone vibrating]

32:11.429 --> 32:12.430
Ah. Take it.

32:17.894 --> 32:18.895
Yes, Mr. Chae.

32:18.979 --> 32:20.772
[gasps, whispers] It's Mr. Chae?

32:22.149 --> 32:23.150
Just a moment.

32:24.818 --> 32:29.865
The materials company he mentioned
will do a material test in a few weeks.

32:29.948 --> 32:33.076
He wants to visit the factory,
and asked if we'll join.

32:33.160 --> 32:34.369
[excitedly] Of course, we should go.

32:34.452 --> 32:36.246
[exclaims, whispers] That's great.

32:36.913 --> 32:38.582
All right, we'll join you.

32:39.332 --> 32:40.458
Okay.

32:41.126 --> 32:42.460
Uh, and, Hyunwoo,

32:43.712 --> 32:47.382
the chance of Ms. Song and I dating…

32:48.216 --> 32:49.217
is zero.

32:49.301 --> 32:50.927
[♪ melancholic music playing]

32:51.011 --> 32:52.804
I thought I should tell you

32:52.888 --> 32:55.974
that there's no need to worry about that.

32:56.933 --> 32:57.934
Okay.

32:59.102 --> 33:00.103
[line disconnects]

33:00.187 --> 33:03.106
I thought you'd keep waiting
for an answer.

33:04.357 --> 33:05.775
You don't have to waste

33:05.859 --> 33:07.569
-your energy on me.
-[elevator dings]

33:13.783 --> 33:14.784
Aren't you getting in?

33:15.869 --> 33:18.663
I left something at home, no, my car.
[chuckles awkwardly]

33:19.456 --> 33:20.749
All right, then.

33:31.092 --> 33:32.177
Zero…

33:34.012 --> 33:35.680
[♪ music fades]

33:35.764 --> 33:37.057
You're getting ready?

33:38.016 --> 33:39.059
Yes.

33:39.601 --> 33:41.311
I'll tell her everything

33:41.853 --> 33:44.272
and apologize to her.

33:44.731 --> 33:45.732
At this rate,

33:46.524 --> 33:48.652
I feel like I'll end up hiding more things

33:48.735 --> 33:51.446
and lying to her even more, so I'm scared.

33:52.030 --> 33:55.075
I want to tell her everything

33:55.158 --> 33:57.953
and love her as my true self from now on.

33:58.995 --> 34:02.332
I want to tell her in my own way
before it's too late.

34:02.415 --> 34:07.504
[doctor] The interruption in your hearing
must be from the stress of lying, too.

34:07.587 --> 34:09.464
You know it yourself

34:09.547 --> 34:12.175
that the truth cannot coexist
with false relationships.

34:12.842 --> 34:16.346
[Haran] It sounds like
they're not meant to be together.

34:16.429 --> 34:18.807
[murmurs] Like the Milky Way and the moon…

34:19.432 --> 34:21.935
These symptoms will occur
more frequently and intensely.

34:22.018 --> 34:24.020
It could end up hurting you badly.

34:24.104 --> 34:26.231
Let's stabilize your condition first.

34:26.314 --> 34:30.360
I'll prescribe a short-term
sedative for you. Ah...

34:30.443 --> 34:32.404
What did the new hallucination sound like?

34:32.487 --> 34:33.488
Ah.

34:33.571 --> 34:36.074
It was sharp, like the sound of metal.

34:36.157 --> 34:38.451
And then something…

34:39.369 --> 34:41.079
like this.

34:41.162 --> 34:43.164
[♪ somber music playing]

34:43.707 --> 34:46.126
I'm not exactly sure what it was.

34:46.209 --> 34:48.086
But I'm worried that... [inhales sharply]

34:48.169 --> 34:50.547
there's something more behind it.

34:50.630 --> 34:52.924
Like the bracelet sounds?

34:53.008 --> 34:56.553
Yes. And if I want
to tell her about myself,

34:56.636 --> 35:00.432
I think I should fill those gaps
in my memory first.

35:00.515 --> 35:01.850
She's connected...

35:03.977 --> 35:05.937
to what happened seven years ago.

35:06.646 --> 35:11.067
Your memories
are like scattered dots right now.

35:11.151 --> 35:14.279
They're not connected,
so you can't understand them.

35:14.362 --> 35:18.074
But once they start getting connected,

35:18.158 --> 35:20.368
they'll start forming a structure,
like this.

35:21.161 --> 35:22.829
And once the gaps are filled

35:22.912 --> 35:25.915
and you understand them yourself,
you'll be able--

35:25.999 --> 35:27.208
To explain myself

35:28.543 --> 35:30.754
to her better.

35:32.464 --> 35:36.217
Do you think there's a way
to fill those gaps?

35:38.303 --> 35:40.013
Mmm. [inhales sharply]

35:40.722 --> 35:42.098
I think so.

35:43.266 --> 35:45.769
Is there anyone else named Sujin

35:45.852 --> 35:49.105
among the staff besides Lee Sujin?

35:49.189 --> 35:50.315
[receptionist] Just a moment.

35:50.899 --> 35:51.900
[sighs]

35:51.983 --> 35:53.985
[♪ music fades]

35:55.654 --> 35:57.447
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

36:05.163 --> 36:06.831
The day of the accident?

36:07.499 --> 36:08.875
Why are you asking me that?

36:10.502 --> 36:12.420
I heard the explosion seven years ago

36:12.504 --> 36:15.465
in Hyeokchan's lab
was caused by a reagent error.

36:16.883 --> 36:18.551
I was just outside the door at the time.

36:19.928 --> 36:22.639
My memories are hazy from the shock.

36:23.765 --> 36:24.933
Do you remember what happened?

36:26.184 --> 36:28.103
I really want to protect something,

36:28.603 --> 36:29.604
but to do that,

36:31.231 --> 36:33.983
I need my memories.
I came to ask you for help.

36:34.776 --> 36:37.028
I wasn't even a student at your college.

36:37.112 --> 36:39.197
I was just a med student
at a school nearby.

36:39.906 --> 36:43.660
I only visited BIT a few times
to meet Hyeokchan, so why…

36:43.743 --> 36:45.620
Whenever I had glimpses
of my lost memories,

36:45.704 --> 36:48.206
I heard the same sound.

36:48.289 --> 36:50.208
-[high-pitched ringing]
-[bracelet rattling]

36:50.291 --> 36:51.710
[Sujin exclaims]

36:51.793 --> 36:54.295
Hey, Sujin. You're here?
I'll head out now.

36:54.379 --> 36:55.588
[Chan] I heard the sound of your bracelet

36:55.672 --> 36:58.717
that you always wore
when you came to see Hyeokchan.

36:59.509 --> 37:00.802
It seemed like a sign

37:00.885 --> 37:04.889
that you're the person
who remembers everything.

37:08.435 --> 37:12.230
I don't know why the gaps in my memories
are connected to you,

37:12.313 --> 37:16.484
but can you tell me what you know
about what happened

37:17.736 --> 37:18.862
seven years ago that I don't?

37:20.363 --> 37:22.657
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

37:22.741 --> 37:24.367
I wrote everything down

37:25.034 --> 37:26.745
whenever I had glimpses of the memories.

37:45.513 --> 37:48.057
-Stop it!
-I'm sorry.

37:48.141 --> 37:49.768
You're in a dangerous state.

37:49.851 --> 37:51.394
-I'm sorry.
-It's not too late.

37:55.565 --> 37:56.858
If there's anything you know…

37:56.941 --> 37:58.651
No, there's nothing.

37:59.235 --> 38:01.571
All I did was exchange
a few words with you.

38:01.654 --> 38:03.031
I'm sorry I couldn't help you.

38:04.115 --> 38:05.116
[Chan] The sound.

38:06.159 --> 38:08.745
Do you know nothing
about the sound I wrote about?

38:09.370 --> 38:10.914
I think it's an important clue.

38:10.997 --> 38:11.998
Uh... [hesitates]

38:12.081 --> 38:14.834
It all started with a sound,
and all these memories--

38:14.918 --> 38:16.044
-[yells] I said I don't know!
-[♪ music fades]

38:16.836 --> 38:18.880
What happened back then still hurts me.

38:19.506 --> 38:21.382
I lost Hyeokchan in that accident.

38:21.883 --> 38:24.719
What's going to change by digging into it?
Someone died.

38:25.678 --> 38:28.181
Why would you torture someone
over just some memories?

38:28.264 --> 38:30.558
You're alive and well right now.

38:30.642 --> 38:32.894
-I…
-I don't know anything,

38:33.436 --> 38:36.272
so don't ever look for me again. [sighs]

38:43.071 --> 38:44.489
[sighs]

38:46.241 --> 38:48.868
Hyeokchan, you left your earphones
in my car…

38:51.538 --> 38:52.539
So you're saying

38:53.206 --> 38:55.834
you kept talking to Haran

38:56.626 --> 38:57.627
while I was away?

38:58.211 --> 38:59.379
Pretending to be me?

38:59.462 --> 39:00.755
[Sujin] Stop it!

39:01.631 --> 39:03.800
[♪ tense music plays]

39:11.724 --> 39:13.935
[♪ music swells, fades]

39:14.018 --> 39:16.813
Genius, won't this look lovely on Chan?

39:16.896 --> 39:18.356
[barks]

39:18.439 --> 39:20.692
[giggling]

39:20.775 --> 39:21.943
You're so cute.

39:22.569 --> 39:24.279
[gasps, chuckles softly]

39:27.574 --> 39:28.575
[gasps]

39:29.200 --> 39:30.535
Where were you?

39:30.618 --> 39:32.829
I didn't call in case you were
having a meeting with Ben.

39:38.960 --> 39:41.421
Hey, why don't you look happy to see me?

39:43.840 --> 39:47.719
I am. I'm so happy, I almost danced.

39:48.720 --> 39:50.096
Is something wrong?

39:50.179 --> 39:51.180
You look troubled.

39:54.851 --> 39:58.021
[Chan groans softly]
I was, because I missed you.

39:58.646 --> 39:59.814
But I came here,

40:00.315 --> 40:03.026
and you're right in front of me.

40:04.027 --> 40:05.987
Then look at me all you want.

40:08.698 --> 40:10.700
[♪ pleasant music playing]

40:15.246 --> 40:17.749
Oh. Why aren't you sitting
in your usual seat?

40:17.832 --> 40:20.793
[Haran] You weren't here,
so I was waiting to see you coming.

40:20.877 --> 40:22.587
-Like a meerkat.
-[Chan chuckles]

40:23.171 --> 40:24.631
What did you sketch? Can I see?

40:24.714 --> 40:25.882
[exclaiming]

40:25.965 --> 40:27.675
[stammering] No, this…

40:27.759 --> 40:29.302
It's a trade secret.

40:29.385 --> 40:31.262
-[chuckles awkwardly]
-[Manjae muttering]

40:32.722 --> 40:35.308
-[exclaims] Let me take those.
-[Manjae exclaiming]

40:35.391 --> 40:38.269
Customers have been asking for blankets,

40:38.353 --> 40:41.230
so I washed them. [chuckles]

40:41.314 --> 40:42.815
You should ask me to do chores.

40:42.899 --> 40:44.859
I should put these in the baskets, right?

40:44.943 --> 40:47.695
-Yes. Thank you.
-No problem.

40:47.779 --> 40:49.322
-[cellphone vibrates]
-Hmm?

40:49.948 --> 40:51.074
[Seok] Happy birthday.

40:51.157 --> 40:54.327
I'm flying out for a seminar,
so I wanted to say it a day early.

40:54.410 --> 40:56.245
I'll treat you for the watch soon.

40:56.329 --> 40:57.330
Birthday?

40:58.998 --> 41:00.249
I should make this soon.

41:01.834 --> 41:03.294
SHIM
Coffee House

41:04.087 --> 41:05.964
Keep your schedule cleared
tomorrow evening.

41:06.047 --> 41:08.132
We're going to dress up
and have a nice dinner.

41:08.216 --> 41:09.425
Sounds good.

41:09.509 --> 41:10.885
Uh, but why all of a sudden?

41:11.636 --> 41:15.098
Uh... I added dressing up

41:15.181 --> 41:17.600
and having a fancy dinner
to the bucket list.

41:17.684 --> 41:19.310
I'll treat you to everything,

41:19.394 --> 41:20.853
and tell you the location later.

41:20.937 --> 41:21.980
Hmm...

41:22.063 --> 41:25.316
-What's going on?
-Anyway, dress up, okay? See you.

41:27.193 --> 41:28.653
[groans] His size…

41:29.988 --> 41:31.239
[giggles]

41:33.825 --> 41:34.826
This is out of the blue.

41:38.371 --> 41:39.372
Uh...

41:39.455 --> 41:42.875
I have a habit of saying goodbye
the American way.

41:44.377 --> 41:46.295
-Since when?
-Starting today.

41:46.379 --> 41:47.422
[Haran giggles]

41:47.505 --> 41:48.589
I'll get going now.

41:52.927 --> 41:54.387
Hmm? [clears throat]

41:57.015 --> 41:59.559
FATHER
HAPPY BIRTHDAY

42:04.063 --> 42:05.064
Gosh.

42:05.648 --> 42:07.066
That was way too obvious.

42:08.026 --> 42:09.068
[chuckles softly]

42:09.152 --> 42:12.905
[doctor] Do you think there's a way
to fill those gaps?

42:15.199 --> 42:17.201
-[♪ music fades]
-[sighs]

42:30.506 --> 42:32.633
-[Yougyum weakly] Hadam.
-Yougyum.

42:32.717 --> 42:34.677
How did you do?

42:36.387 --> 42:38.056
I nailed it.

42:38.973 --> 42:40.099
I kept my promise.

42:40.850 --> 42:42.018
I'm glad.

42:43.186 --> 42:45.313
[breathing shakily] I'm so glad.

42:45.855 --> 42:46.856
Thank you.

42:46.939 --> 42:48.900
They said the surgery went well.

42:48.983 --> 42:50.568
You did it.

42:51.152 --> 42:53.780
I keep feeling sleepy.

42:53.863 --> 42:54.864
Okay.

42:56.199 --> 42:57.909
Sleep. I'll stay with you.

42:58.451 --> 43:00.578
[♪ gentle music plays]

43:01.704 --> 43:04.999
[Yougyum] I'll recover perfectly
and be back on the mound soon.

43:17.470 --> 43:19.472
-[Hadam sniffles]
-[♪ music fades]

43:21.390 --> 43:23.935
Oh, Mr. Yeon, we're heading out now.

43:24.018 --> 43:25.937
See you tomorrow.

43:26.604 --> 43:28.689
-See you tomorrow.
-You're working late again?

43:28.773 --> 43:29.941
Hang in there.

43:30.733 --> 43:33.277
[Raemee] I want to be on Hayeong's team!

43:33.361 --> 43:34.862
-Me too.
-[Seunggyu] Me too, me too.

43:34.946 --> 43:35.947
Me too!

43:36.030 --> 43:38.032
[Hayeong] You all want to pair up with me,
the bowling genius.

43:38.116 --> 43:39.117
[cellphone vibrates]

43:40.368 --> 43:41.661
Yes, Ms. Kim.

43:41.744 --> 43:44.997
[Nana] You postponed the meeting
with Most Korea's editor-in-chief, right?

43:45.081 --> 43:47.458
Yes, I postponed it to next week.

43:48.626 --> 43:52.380
Sorry, but could I ask
where you're going tomorrow?

43:52.964 --> 43:54.298
-I should know
-I'm here…

43:54.382 --> 43:56.259
-to feel more at ease.
-[Nana] Chuncheon.

43:56.843 --> 43:58.219
I'm visiting my hometown.

43:58.302 --> 44:01.139
Don't worry, and call me
if anything urgent comes up.

44:01.222 --> 44:02.306
All right.

44:02.390 --> 44:03.391
You're here.

44:03.474 --> 44:05.476
You cleared your schedule
to go to Chuncheon?

44:05.560 --> 44:06.561
Why Chuncheon?

44:06.644 --> 44:08.062
I want to have some fun, too.

44:09.522 --> 44:12.567
I want to visit
our old neighborhood with Manjae.

44:13.151 --> 44:14.318
I see.

44:15.486 --> 44:17.071
What do you mean, "I see"?

44:18.364 --> 44:19.448
It's nothing. [chuckles]

44:19.532 --> 44:21.367
And you look good in all the scarves.

44:21.450 --> 44:23.161
Your beauty can pull off any color.

44:23.661 --> 44:25.788
But I like the one on the left.

44:26.664 --> 44:28.499
Keep smiling like that. You look pretty.

44:29.458 --> 44:31.752
It's rare to find someone
who makes you smile. Hold onto him.

44:40.094 --> 44:42.513
[inhales sharply] She has great taste.

44:43.848 --> 44:45.057
She really takes after me.

44:45.141 --> 44:46.851
[♪ lively music playing]

44:49.270 --> 44:50.855
Look at this.

44:51.564 --> 44:53.733
All right. Is this better?

44:55.693 --> 44:57.236
-[Manjae scoffs]
-[Genius whines]

44:57.320 --> 44:59.739
-[Manjae] Or this?
-[automated voice] I love you.

44:59.822 --> 45:03.576
[laughs] I know. I love you, too.

45:03.659 --> 45:06.621
But I have to choose
which scarf to wear right now.

45:06.704 --> 45:08.789
Look at them again. Which is better?

45:08.873 --> 45:12.835
[on PA] This train will soon arrive
at its final stop, Chuncheon Station.

45:16.923 --> 45:18.674
Everything's changed.

45:19.467 --> 45:21.052
I can't tell which is which.

45:21.135 --> 45:22.136
[Manjae inhales sharply]

45:23.095 --> 45:27.058
I think… this is where your house was.

45:28.017 --> 45:30.436
Yes, you're right.

45:32.146 --> 45:33.231
But…

45:34.065 --> 45:35.483
our house is gone.

45:36.442 --> 45:37.777
[chuckling] Gosh.

45:37.860 --> 45:39.612
It's been so many years.

45:40.947 --> 45:41.948
[clicks tongue]

45:42.031 --> 45:46.369
Right. Even we've changed this much,
so they can't possibly still be here.

45:46.452 --> 45:48.537
[♪ music fades]

45:48.621 --> 45:49.622
It's here!

45:50.581 --> 45:51.707
The tree's still here.

45:54.585 --> 45:57.129
[Nana] You're right, it's still here.

45:57.213 --> 45:59.590
The persimmon tree my dad planted.

46:00.466 --> 46:01.467
[sighs in relief]

46:02.134 --> 46:03.344
I'm glad

46:04.553 --> 46:05.972
that's still here, at least.

46:08.766 --> 46:10.184
[bell ringing]

46:10.935 --> 46:13.271
[♪ pleasant music playing]

46:13.354 --> 46:14.730
[tires screeching]

46:14.814 --> 46:17.400
Nabong, let's go to school!

46:19.235 --> 46:21.362
I'm going to school!

46:21.445 --> 46:22.571
Manjae! [chuckles]

46:26.367 --> 46:28.619
-All right. Let's go.
-Hold on tight.

46:29.745 --> 46:31.747
[young Nana humming "La Vie En Rose"]

46:33.874 --> 46:36.002
[Nana continues humming "La Vie En Rose"]

46:38.045 --> 46:39.255
-Wow…
-[chuckles]

46:39.338 --> 46:41.966
[laughs boisterously] It's right here.

46:42.049 --> 46:43.801
[Nana] This tree is still here.

46:44.302 --> 46:45.469
[Manjae] It hasn't changed at all.

46:45.553 --> 46:47.722
-[Nana] Come on. Hurry.
-[Manjae exclaiming]

46:47.805 --> 46:48.973
[both laughing]

46:49.056 --> 46:50.349
Right.

46:50.433 --> 46:53.060
-[digital beeping]
-[exclaims]

47:00.651 --> 47:01.694
[camera clicks]

47:03.946 --> 47:05.031
This is so nice.

47:05.114 --> 47:06.157
[both giggle]

47:06.240 --> 47:09.243
Hmm... Hang on, it's untied.

47:09.952 --> 47:10.953
Mmm...

47:14.707 --> 47:15.708
[Nana chuckles]

47:16.459 --> 47:18.377
Ah... [groans] Have some water.

47:19.128 --> 47:21.213
-Manjae, there's something in here.
-Huh?

47:22.214 --> 47:25.092
-[Manjae exclaims]
-[Nana laughs]

47:25.176 --> 47:27.887
I got you! [laughing]

47:28.471 --> 47:31.390
Try and catch me. [giggling]

47:31.474 --> 47:33.476
[birds chirping]

47:34.685 --> 47:36.562
[sighs, sniffles]

47:42.693 --> 47:44.987
-[Manjae laughing]
-[Nana exclaims]

47:45.071 --> 47:46.530
Manjae! My goodness.

47:46.614 --> 47:49.742
-I got my revenge.
-Unbelievable.

47:49.825 --> 47:52.203
[both laughing]

47:52.286 --> 47:53.704
[♪ music fades]

47:53.788 --> 47:56.123
Stay here. I'll go get something warm.

47:56.207 --> 47:57.291
-Okay.
-Okay.

47:59.585 --> 48:00.753
[wind whooshing]

48:01.712 --> 48:02.713
[sighs]

48:14.183 --> 48:16.185
[♪ tense music plays]

48:26.654 --> 48:28.739
[cellphone ringing]

48:33.744 --> 48:34.745
[♪ music fades]

48:34.829 --> 48:38.165
I must've startled you yesterday.
It was the anesthetics.

48:38.249 --> 48:40.918
[inhales sharply] I'm completely fine now.

48:41.001 --> 48:43.129
No, it's the painkillers.

48:43.212 --> 48:46.132
The second day of the bone graft
hurts the most.

48:46.215 --> 48:48.926
The pain in your pelvis
will probably get worse tomorrow,

48:49.009 --> 48:51.387
and you'll barely be able to walk
with crutches

48:51.470 --> 48:53.514
after the drain is removed
on the third day.

48:53.597 --> 48:54.723
-And--
-Wait.

48:55.307 --> 48:58.936
Did I wake after 10 years of sleep
or something?

48:59.520 --> 49:00.896
Did you become a doctor already?

49:00.980 --> 49:03.691
I studied about bone grafting all night.

49:03.774 --> 49:05.443
And here's your plan.

49:06.444 --> 49:07.445
What plan?

49:08.612 --> 49:12.533
A 12-week plan to pass
the New York Comets' physical.

49:12.992 --> 49:15.369
I'm going to help you
with your rehabilitation now.

49:15.453 --> 49:16.454
Huh?

49:16.537 --> 49:19.665
I did well on the CSAT,
and I have time on my hands.

49:20.166 --> 49:22.460
The first step is the hospital treatment.

49:22.960 --> 49:24.086
Focus on recovering,

49:24.170 --> 49:27.047
and once you can move, it's step two.

49:27.131 --> 49:28.340
You'd better brace yourself.

49:28.841 --> 49:30.551
I signed up for the study room again.

49:30.634 --> 49:33.179
I guess I'm getting practice
as a future medical professional.

49:35.222 --> 49:36.223
[yells] Yougyum!

49:36.307 --> 49:37.808
[sobbing] Hey!

49:39.518 --> 49:42.771
Why didn't you tell me
you were getting surgery?

49:42.855 --> 49:46.192
Should I give you some time alone?

49:46.275 --> 49:48.569
-Hey, I'm getting a call.
-[cellphone vibrating]

49:48.652 --> 49:49.653
[chuckles]

49:52.364 --> 49:53.365
Hello?

49:53.449 --> 49:56.702
[woman] Hi, I saw this number
on this woman's necklace.

49:56.785 --> 50:00.039
She doesn't seem to know
where she is right now.

50:00.122 --> 50:02.625
I thought I should let you know.

50:02.708 --> 50:04.418
Uh, right. Just a moment.

50:04.502 --> 50:06.837
[♪ ominous music playing]

50:07.630 --> 50:08.881
Can you buy me some tangerines?

50:08.964 --> 50:13.052
I'm suddenly craving them.
Maybe I need vitamins.

50:13.135 --> 50:14.303
Sure, I'll go buy some.

50:14.386 --> 50:16.847
Yang Changmo, come with me.

50:16.931 --> 50:18.849
I shouldn't leave you with him.

50:18.933 --> 50:22.061
Call me if you need anything else.
I'll get it for you.

50:24.939 --> 50:26.398
Where are you calling from?

50:28.317 --> 50:29.568
Chuncheon?

50:29.652 --> 50:31.570
-[groans]
-[♪ music swells]

50:31.654 --> 50:35.491
Can you stay with her for a moment?
I'll call you back soon.

50:35.574 --> 50:38.702
Have you seen someone like this
on the way here?

50:38.786 --> 50:41.830
You didn't? All right, thank you.

50:42.831 --> 50:45.084
[cellphone ringing]

50:46.502 --> 50:48.587
-Hello?
-Is this Hadam's grandmother's phone?

50:48.671 --> 50:51.298
Are you with Ms. Nana Kim right now?

50:51.382 --> 50:53.175
I'm her youngest
granddaughter's boyfriend.

50:53.259 --> 50:54.260
She was lost,

50:54.343 --> 50:56.720
so someone called and said she's with her.

50:57.429 --> 50:58.597
What?

51:00.307 --> 51:02.893
[Yougyum]
I'm the only one who knows her condition.

51:03.435 --> 51:05.980
Hadam and her sisters don't know yet.

51:06.063 --> 51:08.148
-Hello.
-I called you earlier…

51:08.232 --> 51:09.942
[woman] Ah. Over there.

51:11.986 --> 51:14.446
Ah, yes, thank you.

51:14.530 --> 51:17.032
-[Nana humming]
-[Manjae sighs in relief]

51:20.494 --> 51:21.495
Nabong.

51:23.038 --> 51:24.331
[♪ melancholic music playing]

51:28.919 --> 51:30.254
[nurse] Ms. Kim Nabong!

51:30.337 --> 51:31.797
-Ms. Kim Nabong!
-[Manjae] Wait, Na…

51:31.880 --> 51:33.549
[Nana] I was just visiting a friend there.

51:34.300 --> 51:35.634
I'm going to France soon.

51:39.179 --> 51:40.306
[Manjae] That's what it was.

51:41.432 --> 51:43.559
This is what was happening

51:44.476 --> 51:45.561
to you.

51:45.644 --> 51:47.646
[Nana continues humming]

51:52.026 --> 51:54.194
Nabong, come back to me.

51:54.695 --> 51:55.863
Huh?

51:55.946 --> 51:56.989
It's me,

51:57.698 --> 51:58.741
it's Manjae.

51:59.533 --> 52:01.118
[groans softly]

52:01.201 --> 52:02.328
I'm tired.

52:03.621 --> 52:05.247
I'm so tired.

52:05.331 --> 52:06.832
Okay, get some rest.

52:06.915 --> 52:08.792
Keep resting.

52:09.501 --> 52:10.586
Just rest.

52:17.301 --> 52:19.303
[♪ music fades]

52:29.355 --> 52:31.357
[♪ pleasant music playing]

52:32.858 --> 52:35.736
[Haran] I booked a table here.
Come by 8:00 p.m.

52:36.654 --> 52:37.863
Hmm...

52:38.572 --> 52:40.699
[inhales sharply, exhales] Hmm...

52:40.783 --> 52:42.993
[Haran] You always look nice,
but dress even nicer.

52:43.077 --> 52:44.662
[chuckles softly] This is it.

52:47.164 --> 52:49.333
[doctor] You know it yourself

52:49.416 --> 52:52.211
that the truth cannot coexist
with false relationships.

52:54.004 --> 52:55.047
[sighs]

52:56.548 --> 52:57.800
It's my friend's birthday.

52:57.883 --> 53:00.844
Can you bring that with the candles lit
for the dessert course?

53:00.928 --> 53:02.763
[♪ music fades]

53:02.846 --> 53:03.889
[Hayeong] This much?

53:10.771 --> 53:13.232
Gosh, why does it keep falling?

53:15.275 --> 53:17.611
[creaking]

53:19.029 --> 53:20.030
[snaps]

53:21.824 --> 53:22.950
[exclaims]

53:23.033 --> 53:25.869
[♪ heart-fluttering music playing]

53:38.298 --> 53:39.341
[Taeseok] Your hand.

53:39.425 --> 53:40.843
Are you okay?

53:40.926 --> 53:43.220
Are you hurt anywhere?

53:44.513 --> 53:45.806
I'm fine.

53:46.890 --> 53:47.891
[sighs in relief]

53:49.518 --> 53:51.061
That's a relief.

53:53.188 --> 53:55.023
Ah. Are you okay?

53:55.607 --> 53:56.608
Yes...

54:00.612 --> 54:01.613
I'm fine.

54:06.201 --> 54:08.120
[♪ music fades]

54:08.203 --> 54:10.831
I'll clean up here. You should go.

54:11.498 --> 54:14.251
Don't work so late like you did yesterday.

54:30.184 --> 54:31.685
Let's talk for a moment.

54:33.145 --> 54:35.147
[♪ gentle music playing]

54:44.907 --> 54:46.992
[Chan] I'll be there in five minutes.
See you soon.

54:49.912 --> 54:51.163
[metallic clink]

54:57.836 --> 54:59.588
-[metallic clink echoes]
-[♪ music stops]

55:02.633 --> 55:03.842
[lighter clicking]

55:07.346 --> 55:09.097
[♪ tense music playing]

55:09.681 --> 55:10.933
[static]

55:16.313 --> 55:17.981
[lighter continues clicking]

55:23.278 --> 55:25.948
I'm sorry, but that sound is bothering me.

55:28.450 --> 55:29.451
Sorry.

55:30.410 --> 55:33.247
[lighter continues clicking]

55:39.962 --> 55:41.755
[doctor]
It could end up hurting you badly.

55:41.838 --> 55:42.839
[Haran] And in spring…

55:42.923 --> 55:45.634
It sounds like
they're not meant to be together.

55:45.717 --> 55:46.718
[Sujin] I don't know anything.

55:46.802 --> 55:49.388
[Haran] You always look nice,
but dress even nicer.

55:57.563 --> 55:59.565
[♪ music intensifies]

56:03.819 --> 56:04.820
[groans]

56:16.915 --> 56:17.916
[♪ music fades]

56:21.503 --> 56:24.381
I feel like I should hear
your honest thoughts

56:25.257 --> 56:27.009
to be able to move on.

56:28.885 --> 56:30.721
I have a meeting tomorrow morning.

56:30.804 --> 56:32.931
I have some more work to do--

56:33.015 --> 56:34.641
Just have one glass.

56:34.725 --> 56:35.976
This could be

56:36.602 --> 56:38.020
the last time we talk like this.

56:49.239 --> 56:53.035
How did you know
I've been working late these days?

56:53.118 --> 56:56.204
I don't head out until all the lights
are turned off in the office.

56:56.288 --> 56:58.707
Then what about how you stopped the shelf…

56:58.790 --> 57:01.251
A designer's hands
are their greatest asset.

57:01.335 --> 57:04.588
I only did that to stop you
from getting hurt.

57:04.671 --> 57:07.466
Because I'm a designer at the atelier?

57:10.260 --> 57:11.261
Not because…

57:11.345 --> 57:13.055
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

57:13.138 --> 57:15.182
I'm Song Hayeong?

57:21.730 --> 57:22.731
No.

57:27.361 --> 57:28.820
[Hayeong exhales]

57:30.781 --> 57:32.074
But, Mr. Yeon,

57:32.157 --> 57:33.492
I…

57:34.326 --> 57:36.161
keep misunderstanding such gestures.

57:37.663 --> 57:39.998
You got revenge on Cha Min for me,

57:40.499 --> 57:42.501
brushed off those leaves with your hands,

57:45.462 --> 57:48.674
and told me it's okay to say I'm not okay.

57:51.093 --> 57:53.595
I keep replaying those moments in my head.

57:54.471 --> 57:56.515
So I have to hear it today.

57:56.598 --> 57:59.935
This will keep going on
if I don't hear an honest answer.

58:01.478 --> 58:04.064
Am I really…

58:05.107 --> 58:06.817
just mistaken

58:08.068 --> 58:09.528
about all those situations?

58:12.114 --> 58:13.407
Ms. Kim

58:14.324 --> 58:15.951
is my savior.

58:16.827 --> 58:19.329
And her family, Haran, you,

58:20.163 --> 58:21.248
and Hadam,

58:21.331 --> 58:23.166
are precious to me, too.

58:24.584 --> 58:26.128
I have to protect all of you.

58:27.587 --> 58:29.548
That's why I took care of you.

58:29.631 --> 58:32.384
Even if Haran was in danger,

58:33.176 --> 58:34.428
I would've done the same.

58:35.804 --> 58:37.889
If those moments gave you the wrong idea,

58:39.182 --> 58:40.183
then I'm sorry.

58:43.812 --> 58:47.023
So I guess you're saying

58:47.941 --> 58:51.653
you don't see me as a woman at all.

58:53.655 --> 58:54.656
I'm sorry.

58:56.283 --> 59:00.036
Okay. If you're that firm about it,
then there's nothing I can do.

59:00.620 --> 59:02.539
I don't want to cause you trouble.

59:02.622 --> 59:06.334
I can easily move on and let this go.

59:06.418 --> 59:07.419
Easily.

59:07.502 --> 59:09.296
[♪ music fades]

59:10.338 --> 59:11.423
How about a handshake?

59:12.340 --> 59:15.594
Uh, it would be stupid
for us to grow awkward because of this.

59:15.677 --> 59:18.638
So let's shake hands to end this

59:18.722 --> 59:20.015
on good terms.

59:29.941 --> 59:31.234
[inhales]

59:31.318 --> 59:34.446
[exclaims graciously] You can go now.
You said you have a meeting.

59:35.822 --> 59:37.616
I'm going to eat some of this.

59:37.699 --> 59:39.910
My stomach's been growling for a while.

59:42.913 --> 59:44.122
[driver] I'll start the car now.

59:46.541 --> 59:47.959
Excuse me. Sir?

59:49.544 --> 59:50.712
Oh...

59:50.796 --> 59:52.839
Yes, please go.

01:00:02.098 --> 01:00:03.099
Sir.

01:00:03.934 --> 01:00:06.394
Sorry, but can you open the trunk?

01:00:12.567 --> 01:00:13.568
[sniffles]

01:00:13.652 --> 01:00:15.654
[♪ somber music playing]

01:00:19.574 --> 01:00:21.576
[breathes heavily]

01:00:30.168 --> 01:00:32.087
[whimpers]

01:00:33.213 --> 01:00:34.631
[sobbing]

01:00:43.056 --> 01:00:45.934
[inhales sharply, crying]

01:01:00.907 --> 01:01:03.702
[nurse] How did you hold out
with a fever close to 40 degrees?

01:01:03.785 --> 01:01:06.288
Once the meds kick in,
your fever should come down.

01:01:06.371 --> 01:01:07.455
Get some rest.

01:01:07.539 --> 01:01:08.540
[young Taeseok] Thank you.

01:01:09.499 --> 01:01:10.750
I'm sorry, Ms. Kim.

01:01:10.834 --> 01:01:13.211
I should've driven you on your trip,

01:01:13.295 --> 01:01:15.297
but I shouldn't drive in this state.

01:01:15.380 --> 01:01:18.550
I'll get better soon
and pick you up once your trip's over.

01:01:19.050 --> 01:01:20.176
I'm so sorry.

01:01:20.260 --> 01:01:21.511
[cellphone vibrates]

01:01:22.053 --> 01:01:23.096
[groans]

01:01:25.473 --> 01:01:27.767
DAUGHTER OF KIM NABONG
AND HER HUSBAND HAVE PASSED AWAY

01:01:32.814 --> 01:01:33.815
Sorry.

01:01:35.400 --> 01:01:37.152
[young Hayeong] I have to be okay.

01:01:37.235 --> 01:01:38.904
I have to keep our family together.

01:01:38.987 --> 01:01:40.322
[sighs]

01:01:40.405 --> 01:01:41.615
I have to be okay.

01:01:42.365 --> 01:01:43.700
I have to be okay.

01:01:45.285 --> 01:01:46.328
It's my fault…

01:01:55.086 --> 01:01:56.171
I'm sorry.

01:01:59.591 --> 01:02:01.134
I'm really sorry.

01:02:07.474 --> 01:02:09.809
[♪ music fades]

01:02:10.310 --> 01:02:12.687
[Haran] Where are you?
Why aren't you picking up?

01:02:12.771 --> 01:02:14.064
Did something happen?

01:02:14.147 --> 01:02:15.815
Why can't I reach you?

01:02:15.899 --> 01:02:17.150
I'm getting worried.

01:02:17.233 --> 01:02:19.527
Is there something wrong? [sighs deeply]

01:02:25.033 --> 01:02:26.493
[line ringing]

01:02:27.410 --> 01:02:28.411
[sighs]

01:02:29.371 --> 01:02:30.372
[woman on phone] Hello?

01:02:31.164 --> 01:02:32.165
Hello?

01:02:33.083 --> 01:02:34.125
Who is this?

01:02:41.716 --> 01:02:43.843
[♪ melancholic music playing]

01:02:49.349 --> 01:02:50.350
[Chan weakly] Hey.

01:02:50.892 --> 01:02:51.893
Did you cry?

01:02:52.811 --> 01:02:53.895
I'm okay.

01:02:53.979 --> 01:02:55.689
Let's go to the restaurant.

01:03:00.986 --> 01:03:02.362
I'm really fine.

01:03:02.445 --> 01:03:03.822
Why are you lying?

01:03:04.406 --> 01:03:05.490
You're not okay.

01:03:06.324 --> 01:03:07.993
I heard the doctors talking.

01:03:09.327 --> 01:03:11.579
What's inside your head?

01:03:16.793 --> 01:03:19.671
[doctor] The shrapnel's still lodged deep
in the temporal bone.

01:03:19.754 --> 01:03:23.341
It's right next to the facial nerve,
so there's a high risk of nerve damage.

01:03:23.425 --> 01:03:25.510
These are the follow-up records.

01:03:25.593 --> 01:03:28.513
It went through the petrous part
and even involved the IAC.

01:03:28.596 --> 01:03:30.849
That's how he got his hearing loss.

01:03:30.932 --> 01:03:33.309
Was it the accident
where you lost your hearing?

01:03:34.310 --> 01:03:36.938
If there's something in there,
it's dangerous.

01:03:44.154 --> 01:03:46.614
I'm not someone who will leave
in three months,

01:03:46.698 --> 01:03:49.075
nor someone who might never come back.

01:03:49.784 --> 01:03:50.910
Ms. Song, I want to stay

01:03:52.370 --> 01:03:53.371
with you.

01:03:56.166 --> 01:03:57.667
No, Haran.

01:03:57.751 --> 01:03:58.960
So I'll tell you everything.

01:03:59.044 --> 01:04:01.755
I'll tell you all about the shrapnel
in my head, my ear,

01:04:03.048 --> 01:04:05.717
and about the scars on my body.

01:04:05.800 --> 01:04:07.135
I'll tell you what happened,

01:04:08.136 --> 01:04:11.389
But to tell you everything precisely,

01:04:11.473 --> 01:04:13.058
I need some time.

01:04:13.141 --> 01:04:14.476
It won't take long.

01:04:15.185 --> 01:04:18.146
I'll tell you everything honestly soon.

01:04:19.939 --> 01:04:21.983
I'll lay my heart bare.

01:04:23.068 --> 01:04:25.403
So when I do,

01:04:26.112 --> 01:04:27.489
please listen to everything.

01:04:27.572 --> 01:04:28.573
[exhales]

01:04:29.324 --> 01:04:30.825
What if you're not okay?

01:04:30.909 --> 01:04:32.327
What if something else happens?

01:04:32.410 --> 01:04:35.538
I've been okay, I'm okay now,
and I'll keep being okay.

01:04:35.622 --> 01:04:36.623
So…

01:04:38.166 --> 01:04:39.209
let's go see

01:04:42.128 --> 01:04:44.047
the cherry blossoms in spring.

01:04:44.798 --> 01:04:47.509
We'll have shaved ice in summer,

01:04:47.592 --> 01:04:49.928
see the autumn leaves in fall,

01:04:50.595 --> 01:04:51.805
and in winter…

01:04:53.556 --> 01:04:55.725
it would be fun to go snowboarding.

01:04:56.309 --> 01:04:57.310
[sighs]

01:04:58.311 --> 01:04:59.646
You're awake.

01:04:59.729 --> 01:05:01.606
Could you leave for a moment?

01:05:02.565 --> 01:05:03.650
Stop crying.

01:05:04.692 --> 01:05:06.569
I'll just get checked and leave soon.

01:05:11.116 --> 01:05:13.451
THE SURFACES, BORDERS,
AND TRANSMITTING STRUCTURES

01:05:15.370 --> 01:05:16.955
-[Sujin exclaim]
-[objects clattering]

01:05:17.038 --> 01:05:18.790
[Haran exclaims] Are you okay?

01:05:18.873 --> 01:05:20.625
[Sujin] Gosh. [grunts]

01:05:26.339 --> 01:05:28.341
[♪ tense music playing]

01:05:32.220 --> 01:05:33.721
[Hyeokchan] No, just my roommate.

01:05:33.805 --> 01:05:35.181
[cellphone vibrating]

01:05:43.815 --> 01:05:45.525
-[Sujin] Here.
-Thank you.

01:05:47.152 --> 01:05:48.987
I think you dropped your bracelet.

01:05:51.406 --> 01:05:52.699
This is yours, right?

01:05:57.662 --> 01:05:59.581
[♪ music swells]

01:06:05.628 --> 01:06:08.006
Oh. Hey, crybaby Song Haran!

01:06:08.089 --> 01:06:09.090
[chuckles]

01:06:12.177 --> 01:06:13.178
Hmm?

01:06:14.637 --> 01:06:16.639
[♪ music fades]

01:06:18.057 --> 01:06:20.059
[♪ music intensifies]

01:06:50.715 --> 01:06:52.717
[♪ music fades, ends]

01:06:53.885 --> 01:06:55.887
[♪ uplifting song playing]

01:06:57.388 --> 01:07:00.308
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:07:24.457 --> 01:07:27.126
[Haran] I'll make your birthday
even more special next year.

01:07:27.210 --> 01:07:30.088
I'm going to use that trial
for the rest of my life.

01:07:30.838 --> 01:07:32.924
[Chan]
Don't play around when it comes to her.

01:07:33.007 --> 01:07:34.592
I'm going to make everything okay.

01:07:34.676 --> 01:07:37.136
[Nana sobbing] I'm scared. I'm terrified.

01:07:38.554 --> 01:07:39.931
[Taeseok] I didn't know.

01:07:40.014 --> 01:07:42.892
[Hayeong] Why? How could you not know?

01:07:42.976 --> 01:07:43.977
How about a date tomorrow?

01:07:44.060 --> 01:07:45.895
We can watch a movie, have a nice meal,

01:07:45.979 --> 01:07:48.022
and take a walk while we chat.

01:07:48.106 --> 01:07:49.524
We'll do what other couples do.

01:07:49.607 --> 01:07:51.776
[Haran] Seonu Chan! Where are you?

01:07:51.859 --> 01:07:53.945
I'm so relieved nothing happened.

01:07:57.490 --> 01:07:59.492
[♪ song fades]

01:07:59.575 --> 01:08:01.577
[♪ theme music playing]

01:08:07.458 --> 01:08:08.459
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:08:08.543 --> 01:08:09.544
Translated by Juyoung Park
